# Rally spoiler refinement — 1 November 2026

The Rally car's Touring and Split wing spoilers now mount midway along the sloped hatch, with fitted saddles on the painted pillars beside the rear glass. GT wing, Ducktail and Whale tail receive distinct profile changes; other roof and rear wings retain their own mounting styles. Existing option IDs and stock geometry remain unchanged. The designs take cues from the [Lancia Delta's roof spoiler](https://www.media.stellantis.com/em-en/lancia/press/the-journey-towards-the-lancia-design-day-the-brutal-design-of-stratos-rally-037-and-delta) and the [Ford Escort RS Cosworth's twin wings](https://www.fromtheroad.ford.com/eur/en/articles/2026/ranger-ms-rt-champion-edition-pickup), without incorporating their models or imagery.

The aero mesh cache, both desktop-renderer thumbnail sets and 24 full/simple spoiler modules were regenerated. A category-specific module key rejects previous spoiler modules in packaged builds. The 1,040 non-aero manifest entries and both stock spoiler thumbnails were retained exactly.

With Godot 4.7.2, isolated user data, an empty API URL and `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py`, the source variety, glass-clearance, roll and editing checks passed 814/0. The new actual-mesh hatch saddle test passed 238/0 each for source and prepared parts, with a minimum sampled embed of 1.91 mm. The focused source/module comparison passed 312/0, including 24 actual module hits, material and geometry comparisons. Its initial fixture omitted the stable names normally supplied by the car cache and recorded 24 misses; adding the cache's normal naming step fixed the fixture. The expanded catalogue passed 1,603/0, comparing prepared and source meshes and 13,000 combinations per detail level; maximum full/simple totals remain 169,376/66,420 triangles. Thirty-nine native source showroom captures are under `build/rally-spoiler-personality/final`.

The checks and captures are desktop-only. Reload and owner appearance acceptance remain; the normal build identity and matching prepared-asset rebuild are still needed after concurrent shared-source work settles. No device test, owner-save mutation, live deployment or main-index write was performed.
